# Ezkey mobile — Android build (agents)

When building or installing the React Native Android app, **read `ezkey_mobile/AGENTS.md` § Android debug build** and follow it. Do not trial-and-error `JAVA_HOME`.

When the change bumps React, React Native, Gradle, Android Gradle Plugin, or Kotlin, also read `ezkey_mobile/AGENTS.md` § *Toolchain upgrade gate* and `ezkey_mobile/docs/MOBILE_DEPENDENCY_HYGIENE_CEREMONY.md` § *Cold release gate*. A cached release APK is not proof that `bundleRelease` works.

## First-try command (Git Bash, from `ezkey_mobile/`)

```bash
adb devices -l   # must show a device; abort if empty
corepack enable
./scripts/build-install-debug-clean.sh
```

Equivalent: `yarn android:install:debug:clean`. No device: `--build-only` / `yarn android:assemble:debug:clean`. Prefer `--build-only` then `--skip-clean` (optional `--with-metro-reverse`) to avoid a second full clean Gradle.

## Why agents fail without this

- Maintainer **PATH** often points at **JDK 25** — invalid for RN 0.87 Android Gradle.
- **Android Studio JBR** path varies (`Android Studio` vs `Android Studio1`).
- Long Gradle runs without a prior **`adb devices`** check waste time when wireless adb disconnects.
- Yarn `bash scripts/…` on Windows may hit WSL `System32\bash.exe` — use `run-with-git-bash.mjs` (already wired in package.json).

## JDK rule

Use `scripts/resolve-android-jdk.sh` (JDK 17 preferred; Studio JBR 21 fallback only). Never use repo `C:\Tools\jdk-25*` for mobile Android. Override: `EZKEY_ANDROID_JAVA_HOME`. Do not commit `gradle-daemon-jvm.properties`.

## Shell rule

Use **Git Bash** (`C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe -lc '…'`) for Gradle on Windows, not bare PowerShell `&&` chains for commits/builds.

## Fast path

If `android/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk` exists and only adb dropped: reconnect device, then `./scripts/build-install-debug-clean.sh --skip-clean` (re-applies Metro `adb reverse` when enabled).
